Expected elements: present

Presence check, item by item, all confirmed at 1920x1080: provenance banner first in the shell above the identity bar (badge "Synthetic demo data", chain slug `aztec`, four producer sentences whose tone matches the label); slim identity bar with truncated hash `0xb63616…6359`, `block 101`, and an exit `← aztec` that targets the CHAIN (correct, not a finding); stepping controls in the bar with both directions (◀ ▶ plus step-into/out and jump-to-ends); scrubber at x≈675–935; position readout `128 / 1315`; phase rail; **Code** pane (not Editor) with the current position unmistakable at line 32; Call Trace and Event Log as ONE tabbed region with CALL TRACE open, seven frames, taking the larger share of that column; **Values** pane (not State) below the tabs with fourteen values; TRANSACTION metadata pane. Nothing forbidden: no spinner, no empty pane, no explanatory prose band above the panes, no full-width pane row, Values is not a tab. The NOIR tag is correct here and the cost row reads cleanly as `88000 / 200000 mana (FeeJuice)`.

In register terms the surface is a tool — flush panes, mono chrome, no marketing furniture — but its shared primitives are drawn from two vocabularies at once, and the banner is imported wholesale from the other register. The identity bar itself reads as grouped (identity | controls | scrubber+status | tags), spoiled only by ~330px of void before NOIR.

Highest-priority fixes: redraw the provenance banner as tool chrome, and unify the pane-title face.

Rating: 7/10

